+# R46 B7a allocator accounting — independent Sol LOW check
+
+LENS: Vulkan allocator correctness, production ownership, and evidence integrity
+
+FINDINGS:
+
+1. `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp:4397-4459`, `:1658-1665` | failed bind/map/BDA setup must roll back without ledger/driver divergence | After `allocateMemory()` succeeds, `mapMemory()`, `bindBufferMemory()`, or address setup can throw before `buf->size` and reservation ownership are established. Stack unwinding releases the ledger reservation, but `~vk_buffer_struct()` returns immediately while `size == 0`, so it does not free `device_memory` or destroy `buffer`. The driver allocation remains live while the ledger reports the bytes free and may admit another allocation. This is the maker-disclosed leak window and directly violates transactional accounting. | confidence: h
+2. `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp:1581-1637`, especially `:1604-1607` | test seams must not be able to corrupt production allocator state | Every Vulkan build exports the test seam with `GGML_BACKEND_API`. `ggml_vk_heapres_reset()` clears held test guards and then zeroes the same global ledger used by live buffers, with no test-only build guard, authorization token, quiescence check, or separation from production state. A caller can reset accounting while production buffers remain allocated; later allocations are admitted against false zero usage, and later destruction underflows silently because `vk_heap_reservation::release()` clears `held` before seeing the failed ledger release. Being absent from a public header does not make an exported C symbol safe. | confidence: h
+3. `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp:1448-1450`, `:1525-1528`, `:4356-4397` | accounting must be per actual Vulkan memory heap and general for all Vulkan buffers | The singleton ledger is keyed only by `heapIndex`. Vulkan heap indices are scoped to a physical device, so different GPUs in the same process commonly both have heap 0/1. Their allocations therefore collide in one counter despite having independent budgets and physical heaps, causing false refusals and cross-device releases. The tests model independent numeric heap indices but never model identical indices on separate devices. | confidence: h
+4. `tests/test-backend-ops.cpp:13436-13459`; `r46b-b7a-evidence/14-trace-differential.txt` | tests must exercise production wiring and required exception ownership paths | `ggml_vk_heapres_first_fit()` substitutes only an allocation-failure bitmask; it never executes production `allocateMemory`/map/bind/BDA cleanup. The production trace evidence exercises successful allocation/destruction only. Thus none of the required post-allocation exception paths is tested, and the live defect in finding 1 passes all 38 seam assertions. Add a production-linked fault-injection test that proves both driver-object cleanup and ledger rollback for every fallible stage. | confidence: h
+
+CHECKED:
+
+1. Transactional arithmetic, concurrency, exact fit, cumulative refusal, overflow, underflow, shared heap types, and independent numeric heaps: inspected `vk_heap_ledger` and all `heapres_tests()` assertions; reran `build-vulkan/bin/test-backend-ops.exe heapres` narrowly and observed 38/38 pass, rc 0.
+2. Candidate retry and RAII exact-once behavior: inspected `vk_heap_reservation`, production candidate loop, and seam candidate walk; receipts 02/06/18/21 are green. Receipt 04 is a meaningful planted red (four rollback/destruction assertions fail, rc 1), and receipt 14 distinguishes removed production ownership handoff from clean runs.
+3. Production ownership and destruction: inspected the exact `allocateMemory` through map/bind/BDA/log/handoff sequence and `~vk_buffer_struct`; successful-path ownership is correctly moved only once, but exception cleanup is blocked by finding 1.
+4. Imported path and fallback behavior: inspected imported-host branch and bulk/stock candidate fallthrough. Imported buffers deliberately carry no heap reservation; normal candidate retries release before continuing. No double reserve/release was found in the ordinary successful paths.
+5. Trace gating: every new `reserved=`, `budget=`, and `refuse_budget` emission is inside the existing `alloc_trace` condition. No new unconditional accounting output was found.
+6. Build/CMake/ABI and scope: inspected current diffs and `tests/CMakeLists.txt`; `GGML_USE_VULKAN` is PRIVATE to `test-backend-ops`, the test is registered only under `GGML_VULKAN`, `git diff --check` is clean, and tracked source changes are limited to the three authorized files. Existing unrelated untracked B2 evidence was not attributed to this phase.
+7. Evidence identity: current SHA-256 values exactly match receipt 12 for all three changed files: Vulkan source `97ade68f...`, test source `091bc939...`, and CMake `189f4082...`. Build receipts 01/03/05/15/17/20, correctness receipts 02/04/06/07/08/18/21, and differential receipt 14 are internally consistent. No performance, inference, server, bench, timing, or bandwidth command was run in this check.
+
+NOT CHECKABLE: Driver-level cleanup behavior under injected map/bind/BDA failures is not demonstrated by the supplied receipts; this missing coverage is finding 4. Cross-device heap-index isolation is not exercised by the supplied tests; source inspection establishes finding 3.
+
+BLOCKED
