+# R46 B7a R3 — independent Sol LOW acceptance check
+
+LENS: Vulkan allocator transaction safety, negative-test validity, and evidence integrity
+
+FINDINGS:
+
+1. `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp:1668-1671` | ownership and lifetime comments must describe the enforced safety order accurately | The reservation-member comment still says “The explicit release() at the top of the destructor body is the real guarantee.” R3 deliberately moved that release to the bottom because releasing at the top was the R2 concurrency defect. This stale statement documents the unsafe order immediately beside the corrected implementation and contradicts lines 1674-1693. Update it to state that the device reference outlives the reservation and that the destructor releases only after driver cleanup. | confidence: h
+2. `OPUS-R46-B7A-R3-REPORT.md:8-10`, command table rows 15, 20, and 21 | command/return-code claims must match the retained receipts | The report says “Every command has a `.rc` receipt,” but the production/test symbol census and the two source censuses have no `.rc` files and are shown with em dashes in the report’s own rc column. The four planted reds and all executable/build tests do have correct receipts, so this does not invalidate the repaired red proof; narrow the blanket claim or add receipts for the uncaptured static commands. | confidence: h
+
+CHECKED:
+
+1. Driver-before-ledger ordering: inspected `~vk_buffer_struct()` and the setup guard. Successful destruction performs the driver calls before the unconditional reservation release; exception unwinding destroys driver objects before function-scope reservation rollback. No ledger mutex is held across Vulkan calls, so no new lock cycle was introduced. Explicit release followed by reservation-member destruction is idempotent and does not underflow.
+2. Destruction-order proof: inspected the test-only witness and `ggml_vk_heapres_destroy_order_probe()`. The witness samples the device ledger immediately before `vkFreeMemory`; clean evidence proves the live reservation remains charged and is released afterward. Red C restores release-first ordering, trips both discriminating assertions, and records rc 1.
+3. BDA proof: `VK_TEST_NOTE_BDA()` sits inside the supported-capability block immediately after the real `getBufferAddress()` call. The probe separately returns support and execution witnesses. On this rig both clean BDA assertions pass; Red D deletes the witness, trips both assertions, and records rc 1. The unsupported branch reports BDA coverage unavailable while retaining the separate post-size cleanup check.
+4. Planted evidence: Red C, D, A, and B rc receipts all exist and contain `rc=1`; their outputs show the intended failures. All corresponding planted builds have rc 0. Receipt 11 proves byte-identical source reversion, and three final runs record rc 0 with 69 green assertions.
+5. Prior R2 closures: verified RAII cleanup after allocation, per-device ledger ownership/lifetime, test-owned reset ledger, real production allocator fault injection, driver-usage leak instrument, host double-free deletion, and failure-path trace retirement remain intact.
+6. Production seam isolation: receipt 14 production compile is rc 0; receipt 15 reports zero `heapres`/`vk_test_*` symbols in the production TU and lists the expected test-only symbols in the test-enabled TU. CMake keeps both definitions private and conditional on the Vulkan test target.
+7. Scope, hashes, and validation: current file hashes exactly match receipt 18 (`08a6f483...`, `9672ed08...`, `81eb5770...`); tracked changes remain the authorized three files; `git diff --check` is clean apart from the disclosed line-ending warning. A narrow live `heapres` rerun passed 69 assertions with rc 0. No performance, inference, server, bench, model, timing, bandwidth, throughput, or tuning command was run.
+
+NOT CHECKABLE: The unsupported-BDA reporting branch cannot run on this BDA-capable rig. True two-GPU isolation and imported-host fault cleanup remain structural checks because the available hardware/evidence does not exercise them.
+
+BLOCKED
