+# R46 B7a — Vulkan cumulative heap reservation accounting
+
+You are Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker. Work only in `C:/ArifiLabs/cache/r46b-wt`, branch `lane-230/r46b-rebased-2026-09-11`, HEAD `ae831efde`. You are not alone in the repository: preserve all existing B2 work and raw evidence; do not revert unrelated changes.
+
+## One bounded implementation goal
+
+Implement the first real allocator prerequisite from B7/I7 in `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp`: a thread-safe cumulative per-memory-heap reservation ledger used by Vulkan buffer allocation.
+
+Today `ggml_vk_find_memory_properties()` accepts a memory type when the heap’s total size is at least the single `mem_req.size`; it does not account for allocations already reserved by this process. Add transactional accounting with these semantics:
+
+- Reserve the Vulkan memory requirement size against the selected heap before `allocateMemory`/bind ownership is accepted.
+- Multiple threads cannot collectively reserve beyond the configured usable heap budget; overflow and underflow fail closed.
+- A failed allocation attempt, bind/map/address setup exception, or candidate retry rolls back exactly its reservation before trying another candidate or throwing.
+- A successful buffer owns exactly one reservation record (heap + requirement bytes); `ggml_vk_destroy_buffer()` releases it exactly once. Imported/host paths and fallback candidates must be classified correctly, with no double reserve/release.
+- Selection uses current reserved bytes plus the candidate requirement. Preserve the stock behavior and R46 bulk-large-heap behavior when capacity remains. Do not silently use logical heap index as a physical-channel claim.
+- Emit allocation-trace accounting fields only under the existing trace facility; do not add noisy unconditional output except existing placement receipts.
+
+Keep the mechanism general for all Vulkan buffers, not S-X8-only. This phase does not implement whole-model planning or host splitting/staging reserve; state those as B7b/B7c, not as completed.
+
+## Tests and seams
+
+Add deterministic correctness tests that require no model and no timing. Prefer a small pure accounting seam exercised from an existing Vulkan test target or a narrowly added test mode. Prove at minimum:
+
+1. exact-fit succeeds and one-byte-over refuses;
+2. cumulative reservations across threads cannot exceed budget;
+3. failed allocation/candidate retry rolls back before the next candidate;
+4. successful destruction releases exactly once;
+5. double release/underflow is detected without corrupting the ledger;
+6. two memory types sharing one heap share the same cumulative counter;
+7. separate heaps are independent;
+8. arithmetic overflow fails closed.
+
+A planted defect or deterministic red-first seam must prove the tests can detect missing rollback/release. Do not weaken existing tests or tolerances.
+
+## Hard fences
+
+- Touch only `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp`, the minimum existing test/build-registration files needed for deterministic tests, and new `OPUS-R46-B7A-ALLOC-ACCOUNTING-REPORT.md` plus `r46b-b7a-evidence/**`.
+- No llama-cli/server/bench, model inference, timing, bandwidth, throughput, tuning, or performance runs.
+- Builds and correctness-only unit/backend tests are allowed.
+- Do not fetch/pull/merge/rebase/push/tag/commit, edit board/state, or change environment cadences.
+- Run synchronously; never detach/orphan a build or test. Keep validation narrow and complete within your owned turn. If it cannot complete, stop it and report BLOCKED.
+
+Write the report with inherited HEAD, design invariants, exact files/diffs, commands/return codes, hashes, red-first evidence, remaining B7b/B7c work, and material limitations. End exactly `PHASE-R46-B7A-DONE` only if all required tests pass; otherwise `PHASE-R46-B7A-BLOCKED`.
